% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The checker as a certified program: the decision of
% def:syntactically-grassroots (GSC, Section 3) on a contract given as a term,
% check/2, and the contract as the checker reads it, as_read/2, for a host
% that loads the checker as a compiled module and calls it by dynamic
% activation (TGLP, Section "Module System", "Dynamic Activation"), as the
% Grassroots App does.
%
% A program's entry points are the procedures its self.glp exports, and a
% certificate is refused a program that reaches the person from any of them
% (TGLP, "Compilation", fifth step; IGLP, Program Artefact).  programs/gsc
% exports the printing entries too, compile.glp's and notation.glp's, which
% print to the person; this child directory exports only these two and is
% certified.  Its code is programs/gsc's: these clauses call the checker's
% procedures of programs/gsc/self.glp, its ancestor scope (TGLP, "Implicit
% ancestor scoping"), and programs/gsc forwards its check/2 and
% as_read/2 here, so that each procedure has one copy.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% A contract whose reading has faults is malformed, with them; one whose
% reading has none is decided on what it reads to (check_read/3,
% programs/gsc/self.glp).
exported procedure check(WDeclared?, Verdict).
check(C, V?) :- ground(C?) |
    read_faults(C?, F),
    check_read(F?, C?, V).

% A contract as the checker reads it (programs/gsc/self.glp, the comment
% before as_read_c/2).
exported procedure as_read(WDeclared?, WDeclared).
as_read([], []).
as_read([S|Ss], C?) :- ground(S?), ground(Ss?) | as_read_c([S?|Ss?], C).
as_read(reflexive(Rf, Ss), reflexive(Rf?, C?)) :- ground(Rf?), ground(Ss?) | as_read_c(Ss?, C).
as_read(environment(Ev, B), environment(Ev?, D?)) :- ground(Ev?), ground(B?) | as_read_b(B?, D).
as_read(parametric(Ps, D), parametric(Ps?, R?)) :- ground(Ps?), ground(D?) | as_read(D?, R).
